      </h2>
      <p class="body-text" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Print-on-demand (POD) platforms like Printify and Printful are often presented alongside white label manufacturing as equivalent options. They are not. The business models, product quality, and brand outcomes are fundamentally different.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        POD is appropriate for testing a graphic design concept with zero upfront cost. Bulk white label manufacturing is appropriate for building a real brand with real product quality. Here is why they are different in practice.
      </p>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.83rem; min-width: 560px;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e00;">
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.8rem 1rem 0.8rem 0; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">Factor</th>
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem 0.8rem 0; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">Print-on-Demand</th>
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.8rem 0; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">Bulk White Label (SDF)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {[
              { factor:"Upfront cost",         pod:"Zero",                  wl:"MOQ × per-piece cost" },
